      "summary": "Spread one ripple on the water, seen at a low angle across it: outline-only wide ellipses in thin gray brush, stacked from the inside out, each outer ring's center a little lower so the rings open toward the viewer. Each ring differs a little in width and height, and the lines undulate, narrowly for the inner two and broadly from the third outward. Each outer ring is thinner, the fifth dashed and the sixth dotted as they break up. The whole tilts slightly, up to 3 degrees either way. The written ring count (1–6), or 3–5 when none is written. It sits at one of five positions in the lower half of the canvas."
